+
+```python
+# Discover available record families.
+families = ws.list("/proc")["entries"]
+
+# Find candidate JSON records under a family named by sqlite_schema.txt.
+paths = ws.find(root="/proc/<family>", name="", kind="files", limit=50)["paths"]
+
+# Read and parse one record.
+obj = json.loads(ws.read(paths[0])["content"])
+```
+
+Use `ws.find`/`ws.list` to narrow to the relevant family and record set, then
+read JSON records with `ws.read` and `json.loads`. The recovered schema names
+families and fields; it is not a promise that the same names work in SQL.
